===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|collective|or|in the plural}} That which is of the earth or earthly; a terrestrial being.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=Tamar M. Boyadjian|title=The City Lament: Jerusalem across the Medieval Mediterranean|city=Ithaca & London|publisher=Cornell University Press|page=28|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=XzdtDwAAQBAJ&dq=earthly&pg=PA28|passage=He claims that the book directs the believer to let go of the '''earthly''' and await God's kingdom in the heavenly.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=[1844]|author=Elizabeth Barrett Browning|chapter=The Virgin Mary to the Child Jesus|title=Mrs. Browning's Poems with Memoir|city=Chicago & New York|publisher=Henneberry|stanza=5|page=267|pageurl=https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=inu.32000000341836&view=1up&seq=295|passage=So, let all '''earthlies''' and celestials wait / Upon Thy royal state! / Sleep, sleep, my kingly One!}}
#* {{seemoreCites|en}}
# {{lb|en|UK|colloquial}} A [[slightest]] [[chance]] (of success etc.) or [[idea]] (about something).
#* {{RQ:Doyle Land of Mist|passage=He arched his eyebrows over the summons. "The poor devil has not an '''earthly'''!" said he. "He's lucky to have a summons. Usually they act on a warrant."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1974|author={{w|GB Edwards}}|title=The Book of Ebenezer Le Page|page=315|year_published=2007|location=New York
|passage=‘Then I didn't have a chance when I stood you a drink?’ I said. ‘Not an '''earthly'''!’ she said and laughed; but when I left she kissed me good-night.}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# in an [[earthly#Adjective|earthly]] [[manner]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Midsummer Q1|act=I|scene=i|page=6|passage=But '''earthlyer''' happy is the roſe diſtild, / Then that, vvhich, vvithering on the virgin thorne, / Grovves, liues, and dies, in ſingle bleſſedneſſe.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1827|title=Tales; Mournful, Mirthful, and Marvellous|volume=3|author=Sarah Wilmot Wells|page=94|oclc=|passage=and dost thou, indeed, revive to existence only to again (even in more attempered blood) design the death of the innocent, helpless, orphaned memorial of a pure, a heaven and '''earthly'''-sanctioned flame, whose venial trespass was but the forestalment of your own decree?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1886|title=Reason and Revelation, Hand in Hand|author=Thomas Martin McWhinney|page=324|oclc=|passage=And here again we observe the great advantage of the heavenly over the '''earthly''' appointed courts.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1927|title=The Message of Aquaria|author=Harriette Augusta Curtiss|page=431|oclc=|passage=Under such circumstances it is wise that church and state be separated, for such an '''earthly''' ordained priesthood has no more ability to rule wisely than have civil rulers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|title=Jimmy Swaggart: the Anointed Cherub That Covereth|author=Patricia Ann Sunday|page=1|isbn=|passage=The Lord has allowed me to see a striking similarity between this heavenly anointed cherub and this '''earthly''' anointed cherub (messenger) of God.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|title=The Way of Grace|author=Bruce W. Hubbard, Marlene Hubbard|page=|isbn=|passage=Qualifications are heavenly ordained, not earthly appointed; it is God Who has qualified us as saints and made us fit to share in His eternal salvation. It is not our own efforts and accomplishments that have qualified us; {{...}}}}

